# Why the tests are not excluded outright.
#
# This file used to ignore `test/` wholesale, because the detector fires on
# synthetic credentials in the test suite — `s3cret`, `hunter2-secret`,
# `token = content["access_token"]` — and a gate that fires on a test's own
# fixtures is a gate people learn to bypass.
#
# But excluding the whole directory means a real credential pasted into a test
# is never looked at, and tests are exactly where somebody pastes a value to
# reproduce a bug. That trade is only safe while nobody does it, which is not a
# property anyone checks.
#
# So the directory is scanned. Measured on the current suite: one finding, at
# 0.70 confidence, on the *name* of a test function
# (`test_a_normal_multi_page_walk_is_untouched`) — a detector that read
# `test_boundaries` as an encoded token. No test contains anything resembling a
# real credential.
#
# The finding is left visible rather than baselined, deliberately. A baseline
# marks findings as accepted, and spending it on this would also silence
# anything real that later appeared in the same file. It sits at `low`, so it
# does not block commits at `fail_on: high`, and it is the honest state: a real
# finding in a test would still be reported and would still block.

# Example values in the commented-out starter config.
.minesweep.yml